nd the review threat model WI-860 states (by link); the verdict rules each finding FIX, DISMISS (out of scope, refuted, or not worth its cost, with the reason) or ESCALATE (high risk, to the owner), and is validated like the other classes. The class and its verdict grammar are built once, here, for WI-811's loop sitting to reuse.\n- The coordinator's in-lane cycle routes to it: a finding the builder or coordinator contests, and any finding class reaching its third review round, goes to the dispute sitting before another build round; the ruling's path is recorded in the lane's decisions record, and a dismissed finding is not re-raised to the builder.\n- The coordinator-cycle skill (WI-848, if landed) states the route in place of rules 2 and 3's interim procedure.\n- The spine carries the obligation (Terra authors it; an independent adjudicator judges it in the lane).\n- Review bar: A (one cross-family REVIEW-A).\n- RESYNC_PACK: an entry anchored at a trunk commit (a shipped brief template is added).\ncommit 59f628da7883749836bd3e9210b693018364e14e\n    build: WI-865: the coordinator's adjudication entry point rules a contested or repeated review finding\n    \n    A `dispute` brief class on the shared composition, binding, verdict and\n    telemetry path: the brief carries each finding and the builder's or\n    coordinator's position verbatim (a strict TOML findings file), the lane\n    range, and the review threat model by link to PROCESS.md §6; the one\n    verdict parser (kitlib/dispute.py) rules each finding FIX, DISMISS\n    (out-of-scope | refuted | not-worth-cost, with a reason) or ESCALATE, and\n    refuses an unruled, duplicate, unrequested or malformed ruling. The\n    session-protocol skill routes a contested or third-round finding to it.\n    The dispute brief joins FINDING_JUDGING_BRIEFS; `dispute` joins this\n    repo's retain_for. RESYNC entry anchored at 52d3d88d. Built by Claude\n    Opus (kit-builder); the coordinator re-ran the affected modules (329\n    passed, 1 skipped).\n    \n    WI: WI-865\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n .agents/skills/session-protocol/SKILL.md           |  12 ++\n .claude/skills/session-protocol/SKILL.md           |  12 ++\n docs/declared-absences                             |   1 +\n docs/process.toml                                  |   6 +-\n project-trajectory/RESYNC_PACK.md                  |  28 +++\n project-trajectory/prompts/CATALOG.md              |   1 +\n project-trajectory/prompts/README.md               |   1 +\n .../prompts/adjudicate-dispute.template.md         |  62 ++++++\n project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py     |  88 +++++++-\n .../scripts/coordinator_adjudicate.py              |   9 +-\n .../scripts/kitlib/bootstrap_manifest.py           |   8 +\n project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/dispute.py       | 230 ++++++++++++++++++++\n project-trajectory/scripts/prompts.py              |   6 +-\n .../skills/session-protocol/SKILL.md               |  12 ++\n tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py                     |  13 +-\n tests/test_coordinator_adjudicate.py               |  60 ++++++\n tests/test_dispute.py                              | 238 +++++++++++++++++++++\n tests/test_prompts.py                              |   6 +-\n tests/test_session_keep.py                         |   6 +-\n 19 files changed, 776 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)\ncommit 48c33ddc52b63c1abe21bf1088fb3a18cfbc9497\n    spine: WI-865 change set: SR-234 states the dispute ruling; LLR-314, LLR-315, IF-290 and TC-334 carry and verify it; SR-233's chain admits the dispute brief","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
